  This patch is to fix multiple dangling prompt bugs.  

  These bugs take the form of an "In what direction?" prompt
being displayed when the program will actually interpret
a direction key as a request for player movement/attack.



  Most of the changes replace code of the form:

 	if(!getdir((char *)0)) return 0;

  With:

        if(!getdir((char *)0)) {
            pline(Never_mind);
            return 0;
        }


  Note that the actual functional change consists of adding
"pline(Never_mind);" when getdir does'nt return a direction.


  An exception to this is in the code for throwing objects.  When
the thrown object doesn't hit anything that gives a message, the
text "Missed" is displayed in order to remove the get direction
prompt from the screen.


  To deactivate the patch, remove "#define PROMPT_FIX" from 
config.h and recompile.


  For a fuller discussion of the bugs see:
http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/msg/04b418d84abf545d?dmode=source&hl=en


